# ── Chapter 14 fidelity pins: "Holding a Role in Somebody's Life" ──────────
#
# KIND: CONTENT pin. Run:
#   ./verify.sh --only book-1/14-holding-a-role-in-somebodys-life.pins.nibli
#   ./verify.sh          # all substantive pins and contradiction checks
#
# The chapter's case lists tests/pins/records/child_with_nobody/fixture.nibli
# and tests/pins/family-life/initiation/positive/fixture.nibli.
#
# The ordinary half is its own constitution block beside the barriers rather
# than a rewrite of them, and its positive records have their own cases:
#   tests/pins/family-life/role/positive
#   tests/pins/family-life/participation/positive
#   tests/pins/family-life/support/positive
#   tests/pins/family-life/interpretation/positive
#   tests/pins/family-life/continuity/positive
#   tests/pins/family-life/reproductive/positive
#   tests/pins/family-life/directive/positive
#   tests/pins/family-life/origin/positive
# and the sequences that are the claims this chapter actually makes:
#   tests/pins/family-life/life-course/continuity-needs-no-family-role
#   tests/pins/family-life/life-course/support-is-not-substitution
#   tests/pins/family-life/life-course/interpretation-without-support-first
#   tests/pins/family-life/life-course/role-does-not-travel-between-domains
#   tests/pins/family-life/life-course/own-record-access-confers-no-relationship
#   tests/pins/family-life/life-course/role-defect-and-rights-sequence
# Nothing there decides best interests, capacity, consent, pregnancy,
# parentage or death, and no age is supplied.
#
# WHAT FALSE MEANS HERE: a FALSE is pinned only where the KB could have said
# TRUE, and the comment says what would flip it.

:expect-pins 32

# ── "The barriers hold for Nell as for everyone" ───────────────────────────
# The barriers this chapter renders, asked of a record of one line. Each has
# person($x) as its whole body, which is why a child with nobody reaches them.
? prevents(Nell, PublicFirstCareContinuity).
# => TRUE

? prevents(Nell, KinshipNoPersonalCareDebt).
# => TRUE

? prevents(Nell, DependantIndependentRights).
# => TRUE

? prevents(Nell, ChildIndependentRights).
# => TRUE

? prevents(Nell, ChildAccessibleInformationHelp).
# => TRUE

# "The person must be heard without a minimum speaking age."
? prevents(Nell, ChildVoiceNoAgeFloor).
# => TRUE

? prevents(Nell, ChildSeparationLastResort).
# => TRUE

# "The last resort is reached only through the step before it."
? prevents(Nell, SupportBeforeRemoval).
# => TRUE

# A missing kinship record never certifies independence: independence needs
# a positive entry.
? prevents(Nell, MissingKinshipNoIndependence).
# => TRUE

# "a family's absence authorises no confinement"
? prevents(Nell, FamilyStatusNoConfinement).
# => TRUE

? prevents(Nell, HouseholdNonprescription).
# => TRUE

? prevents(Nell, StatusNoHarmPresumption).
# => TRUE

# "A record of care as employment identifies an activity and nothing more":
# it shows no care reaching anyone.
? prevents(Nell, CareStatusNondelivery).
# => TRUE

? prevents(Nell, Book2LifeCourseBoundary).
# => TRUE

# ── The debt stands without any private route ──────────────────────────────
# "The State owes Nell care and company while the record shows neither
# delivered." The debt is unmoved by the absence of every private route.
? owe(State, Healthy, Nell).
# => TRUE

? owe(State, Meets, Nell).
# => TRUE

# No receipt shows care or company reaching the child, so neither follows.
? healthy(Nell).
# => FALSE

? meets(Nell).
# => FALSE

# ── "no family, household, association or charity is presumed to supply the
# floor" — the record holds none of them for this child. ───────────────────
? family(Nell).
# => FALSE

? home(Nell).
# => FALSE

# ── Adulthood and missing evidence ─────────────────────────────────────────
# "Cira is a person and is owed the floor." Without adulthood evidence "the
# rules stop short of a ballot conclusion", an absent premise rather than a
# finding: "That settles nothing about Cira's age."
? person(Cira).
# => TRUE

? decide(Cira, Ballot).
# => FALSE

# ── When nobody holds a role at all ──────────────────────────────────────────
# The reviewed appointment, run from tests/pins/family-life/initiation/positive.
# Three separately authorised people agree on every field; the representative is
# none of them and is not the person; the appointment names a receipt witness
# the acting body is obliged to authorise.
? complete(LifeCourseCaseRecord, ReviewedAssistanceInitiation, LifeCourseCaseDecision).
# => TRUE

# "The representative owes action within the appointed matter; the office
# that hears challenges owes a hearing and correction."
? obliged(LifeCourseCaseRepresentative, ActForThePersonWithinTheAppointedMatterOnly, LifeCourseCaseRecord).
# => TRUE

? obliged(LifeCourseCaseReader, HearTheChallengeToTheAppointmentAndCorrectIt, LifeCourseCaseRecord).
# => TRUE

# "When the appointment completes, the acting body owes a duty to authorise
# that witness, and the appointment itself leaves the witness unauthorised."
? obliged(LifeCourseCaseActor, AuthorizeTheNamedReceiptWitnessForThePerson, LifeCourseCaseRecord).
# => TRUE

? authorized(LifeCourseCaseWitness, DeliveryWitness, LifeCourseCaseParticipant).
# => FALSE

# "completes only for someone a standing encounter has reached" — the fixture's
# first-contact entry is what makes the participant a person; the generated
# initiation/without-standing case removes it and nothing completes.
? person(LifeCourseCaseParticipant).
# => TRUE

# The representative acts for "that matter alone, as distinct from a guardian
# over the person's life": the appointment "concludes nothing adverse about
# the participant" and "gives the representative no parentage authority".
? false(LifeCourseCaseParticipant).
# => FALSE

? authority(LifeCourseCaseRepresentative, Parentage, LifeCourseCaseRecord).
# => FALSE

# ── The child with nobody, and the duty that needs no request ────────────────
# Article 1c reads personhood alone, so it holds for a record of one line while
# no appointment record exists for that child at all.
? obliged(RightsAdvocate, InitiateAssistanceAndRepresentationWithoutARequest, Nell).
# => TRUE

? complete(Nell, ReviewedAssistanceInitiation, Nell).
# => FALSE
